      "id": "CADTRACK-SMOKE-RECEIPT-NATIVE-IDENTITY-NOT-BOUND",
      "severity": "BLOCKER",
      "title": "Full admission does not prove its smoke receipt/native status belongs to the drafted smoke job",
      "source": "scripts/eval_cadtrack_ep20_baseline.py:52-62",
      "evidence": "In the full path, admission binds the smoke receipt and native status only by file SHA, then checks receipt stage/checkpoint/11 frames/state_unchanged and native COMPLETE/exit_code=0. It does not compare receipt.task or native.task to plan[\"smoke\"][\"task\"], and does not bind native.command and native.physical_gpu to the smoke run config and plan[\"smoke\"][\"gpu\"]. A successful but mismatched/stale smoke artifact can therefore satisfy these checks.",
      "minimal_required_fix": "In the full admission branch, load the smoke run config, verify receipt.config_sha256 against it, then require receipt.task and config.task and native.task to equal plan[\"smoke\"][\"task\"], native.command to equal config.native_command, and native.physical_gpu == config.physical_gpu == plan[\"smoke\"][\"gpu\"]. Also require smoke_only=true, exploratory_test=false, and test_eligible=false on the receipt.",
      "launch_consequence": "Do not admit or launch full TEST jobs until these smoke-to-full identity checks are enforced."
    }
  ],
